{"base_commit": "30f8f89ebb84c0f6153979796d1c0cbd65af8eeb", "issue_body": "This is an attempt to fix the bug described in #3167.

It appears that when enabling the CV-X-IF interface while disabling the RVC extension, the core freezes during the initialization phase of the debug sequence in the testbench.

I managed to find out that this was caused by a bug inside the Decode stage: the compressed‑instruction channel driver of the CV-X-IF inside the Decode stage is only generated if the RVC extension is enabled. However, this module still drives signals inside the stage even when RVC is off. I proposed a fix in the PR below, although I am not sure it is the cleanest way to address the issue.", "issue_title": "Fix a bug that causes the core to freeze when enabling CV-X-IF while disabling RVC extension", "previous_actions": [], "repository": "openhwgroup/cva6", "tool_context": {"benchmark_level": "RTL_BUG_FIX", "bug_scope": "RTL_CONFIG_INTEG", "reproducer_path": "existing_dv", "reproducer_signal": 1, "simulation_cost": 1}}

{"base_commit": "a5e1e76a549272979bb98b5ae1978a7f378e3017", "issue_body": "This PR is to fix the https://github.com/openhwgroup/cva6/issues/3163 and https://github.com/openhwgroup/cva6/issues/3190. 

This fix has prohibited the result of the instruction with exception from being forwarding to subsequent instructions in the scoreboard. This ensures that the kernel-space data cannot be transmitted to the user-space code, thereby preventing the secret from being encoded into the microarchitecture.

By invalidating the corresponding [`fwd_res_valid`](https://github.com/openhwgroup/cva6/blob/master/core/issue_read_operands.sv#L541) entry for the scoreboard entries with exceptions, it is possible to defend against attacks of Meltdown, Spectre and their variants.", "issue_title": "Fix the Meltdown and Spectre vulnerabilities that break the isolation between user-space and kernel-space", "previous_actions": [], "repository": "openhwgroup/cva6", "tool_context": {"benchmark_level": "RTL_BUG_FIX", "bug_scope": "RTL_LOGIC", "reproducer_path": "full_chip_sw", "reproducer_signal": 2, "simulation_cost": 2}}

