{"base_commit": "0185b840159887dfc1460e09a306d3b292934339", "issue_body": "Due to the relocation of the 1-4-bit packer FIFO, the main SM done signal arrived one cycle too early in the single lane mode. This caused the SHA3 process_i signal to go high one cycle too early. This in turn caused the issue that the last word from the precon FIFO is not absorbed properly by SHA3.
This commit fixes this by delaying the main_sm_done signal by 1 cycle in the single lane mode. The ht_error signal has to be delayed by 1 cycle as well to guarantee that the error signal arrives at the same time as the main_sm_done signal.

Resolves #23773", "issue_title": "[entropy_src/rtl] Delay the main_sm_done signal", "previous_actions": [], "repository": "lowRISC/opentitan", "tool_context": {"benchmark_level": "RTL_BUG_FIX", "bug_scope": "RTL_CONFIG_INTEG", "reproducer_path": "existing_dv", "reproducer_signal": 1, "simulation_cost": 1}}

{"base_commit": "998d6472cfa4ef0854187399d976e81d191f764f", "issue_body": "The decision whether a command is invalid is taken based on the command header but EDN might continue and send the additional data as well (it might already be in the FIFO). Previously, CSRNG would just pop the invalid command header from the FIFO and leave any additional data in the FIFO which can then erroneously be interpreted as the next command header.

Instead, we have to absorb the full invalid command before we can continue. This commit modifies the design to keep emptying the FIFO until the command interface is idle.

This is related to lowRISC/OpenTitan#23526.", "issue_title": "[csrng] Flush command FIFO after signaling ACK errors", "previous_actions": [], "repository": "lowRISC/opentitan", "tool_context": {"benchmark_level": "RTL_BUG_FIX", "bug_scope": "RTL_INTERFACE", "reproducer_path": "existing_dv", "reproducer_signal": 1, "simulation_cost": 1}}

{"base_commit": "27279ff687cb16bf10fa5c9748d2b1aed4ede5cf", "issue_body": "Previously, these errors would trigger a fatal alert but not cause a local escalation (i.e. lock up the main SM). Since these FSM errors are structural errors that can't occur e.g. due to how the module currently operates but instead due to FI attacks only, these errors should also cause a local escalation.

This change better aligns CSRNG with EDN and ENTROPY_SRC.

This is related to lowRISC/OpenTitan#19789.", "issue_title": "[csrng] Locally escalate upon FSM errors", "previous_actions": [], "repository": "lowRISC/opentitan", "tool_context": {"benchmark_level": "RTL_BUG_FIX", "bug_scope": "RTL_SPEC", "reproducer_path": "existing_dv", "reproducer_signal": 2, "simulation_cost": 1}}

